//     `mysql`/`sys`/`performance_schema` system schemas, and — being a db-scoped
//     grant — to FILE/PROCESS/SUPER (so no LOAD_FILE / INTO OUTFILE file reads).
//     `information_schema` stays readable but MySQL filters its rows to objects
//     the connecting user can see, i.e. this account's own databases. The app
//     ALSO validates the target db belongs to the account (defence in depth), but
//     even a bug there cannot breach the grant.
//
//   * PROTOCOL-LEVEL TRANSPORT — NO `mysql` CLI, EVER. The customer's SQL is run
//     through the `mysql2` protocol driver, which speaks the MySQL wire protocol
//     directly. It is NOT a command-line client, so it has NO in-band
//     meta-command interpreter: `\!` (shell-out), `\.`/`source` (read a node
//     file), `\T`/`tee` (write a node file) are CLI-only constructs and are sent
//     verbatim to the server as ordinary (invalid) SQL — they never execute on
